0. Your role and how to work
You are a senior full-stack engineer and product designer. Build a production-ready, self-hosted e-commerce platform for a Bangladeshi online store that sells natural/organic food (honey, ghee, oils, dates, nuts, seeds, rice, spices, tea). The store name is <STORE_NAME> and the domain is <DOMAIN>.

The platform has two parts:

Storefront. A fast, mobile-first shop for customers.
Admin dashboard. Modelled on the WordPress + WooCommerce admin (left sidebar, list tables with status filters, bulk actions, edit screens with side boxes). It must be complete enough that the owner never needs to touch code to run the business: products, images, banners, menus, pages, couriers, payments, SMS, tracking codes, webhooks, staff and settings are all managed from the UI.
Working rules:

Work in the phases listed in section 14. At the end of each phase, run the app, run the tests, and give a short summary of what works.
Never leave placeholder "TODO" features in shipped screens. If something needs an external account (courier API key, SMS key, payment merchant), build the full integration and settings screen, and make it work in sandbox/test mode until real keys are entered.
Write clean, typed, documented code. Add seed data that looks real (Bangladeshi names, phone numbers, districts, products in ৳).
Ask me only when a decision truly changes the product. Otherwise choose sensible defaults and list them in DECISIONS.md.
1. Tech stack and architecture
Framework: Next.js (latest stable, App Router) + TypeScript, server components where useful.
Styling: Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui (Radix) for admin components. Use CSS variables for every design token so the theme is editable from the admin.
Database: PostgreSQL with Prisma ORM. All money stored as integers (poisha) or Decimal; never floats.
Cache / queues: Redis + BullMQ for background jobs (webhooks, courier sync, SMS, emails, feed generation, image processing, scheduled sales).
Auth: Auth.js (NextAuth) or Lucia. Customers log in with phone + OTP (SMS) and optionally email/password or Google. Staff log in with email + password + optional 2FA (TOTP).
File storage: S3-compatible (Cloudflare R2 / AWS S3 / local disk adapter for VPS). Image processing with sharp: auto-convert to WebP/AVIF, generate sizes (thumb 150, card 400, product 800, zoom 1600), strip EXIF, keep originals.
Search: PostgreSQL full-text with Bangla + English support (trigram for typo tolerance). Optional Meilisearch adapter.
Email: SMTP / Resend adapter. SMS: pluggable provider adapters (section 8).
Deployment: Docker Compose (app, worker, postgres, redis, nginx/caddy), works on any VPS (e.g. Hostinger VPS) and on Vercel + managed Postgres. Include .env.example, health check endpoint, migration and seed scripts, and daily DB backup job.
Testing: Vitest for units, Playwright for end-to-end (full checkout, order confirmation → webhook fired, courier booking in sandbox, admin permissions).
Code layout: /app/(store), /app/(admin)/admin, /app/api, /lib (domain services), /workers, /integrations/{couriers,payments,sms,ads}, /prisma.
Public REST API (/api/v1) with API keys and scopes, plus outgoing webhooks, so other tools can read orders/products.
