5. Order lifecycle (business rules)
Customer places order → status Pending; stock reserved; purchase pushed to the dataLayer in the browser; customer gets "order received" SMS; admin gets a new-order alert.
Agent calls the customer. Outcomes: Confirm, On hold (no answer; auto-reminder; after N failed attempts auto-cancel if enabled), Cancel (reason required), Fake/Spam (blocks phone, optionally IP).
On Confirmed: stock deducted, confirmation SMS sent, conversion webhook fires (section 9.4), optional auto-booking to the default courier.
Processing → Ready to ship (packed, label printed) → Shipped (courier consignment created, tracking ID saved, SMS with tracking link) → courier status sync updates Out for delivery / Delivered / Returned / Partially delivered automatically.
Delivered: COD amount marked collectable; review-request SMS after N days; optional OrderDelivered webhook.
Returned/Cancelled after confirmation: stock restored (or sent to damaged stock), optional OrderCancelled webhook so ad platforms can be adjusted, refund flow if prepaid. Every transition is logged with staff name and time. Allowed transitions are enforced, with an admin override.
6. Customer-facing communications
SMS on: order placed, confirmed, shipped (tracking link), delivered, cancelled; OTP; abandoned cart; back in stock; review request. Emails with the same events if an email is given. All templates editable in Bangla and English in the admin.

7. Courier integration (one click, like WooCommerce courier plugins)
Build a pluggable courier adapter system (/integrations/couriers/<name>), each implementing the same interface: testConnection(), getCities/Zones/Areas() (if the courier needs location IDs), createParcel(order), bulkCreate(orders), getStatus(trackingId), cancelParcel(), getDeliveryCharge(…), getBalance()/payments (if available), handleWebhook(payload), fraudCheck(phone) (if available).

Ship adapters for the main Bangladeshi couriers, using each courier's official merchant API documentation (read it; don't guess endpoints):

Steadfast Courier (API key + secret key; create order, bulk create, status by consignment ID / invoice / tracking code, balance).
Pathao Courier (OAuth client ID/secret + merchant credentials; store ID; city → zone → area IDs; create order, price calculation, status webhooks).
RedX (API token; areas; create parcel; tracking; webhooks).
Paperfly, eCourier, and a "Manual / Other courier" option (enter courier name + tracking ID by hand, with a tracking URL template).
Admin features:

Couriers → Accounts: connect each courier (credentials, sandbox/live toggle, default pickup store/address, test connection button, status: connected / error).
Location mapping: our districts/areas mapped to each courier's city/zone/area IDs (auto-suggest by name, manual override, saved per order).
One-click "Send to courier" on the order screen and in bulk from the order list. A pop-up lets staff confirm or change courier, COD amount (auto = order due amount), weight, item description, delivery type and note; then it creates the parcel and stores the consignment ID, tracking code, courier delivery charge on the order, sets status to Shipped, and sends the tracking SMS.
Auto-booking rules (optional): e.g. "When an order is Confirmed and district is Dhaka → Pathao; otherwise → Steadfast".
Status sync: receive courier webhooks where supported, and poll the rest every 30–60 minutes via the job queue. Map courier statuses to our statuses (configurable mapping table).
Bookings list: all parcels with courier, tracking, status, COD, charge, date; filters; re-sync and cancel buttons; error list with the courier's error message.
Labels: print courier labels/our 4×6 labels with barcode, in bulk.
COD reconciliation: import or fetch courier payment reports, match to orders, show collected vs pending vs mismatched amounts, mark orders as paid.
Fraud / delivery-success check by phone: call couriers' fraud-check endpoints where available plus our own history; show "X of Y delivered (Z%)" with a colored badge on the order list, order screen, incomplete orders and checkout risk rules (e.g. auto-hold if success < 50%).
Logs of every courier API request/response (secrets masked).
