9. Tracking specification (must be implemented exactly)
9.1 Google Tag Manager without code edits
Admin → Settings → Tracking: toggle "Enable GTM", field Container ID (GTM-XXXXXXX, validated). From the ID, generate the official GTM <head> snippet and the <noscript> body snippet and inject them on every storefront page (head snippet as high as possible in <head>; noscript right after <body>).
Optional override fields: paste full <head> code and paste full <body> code. If filled, they replace the generated snippets. This supports server-side GTM / custom loader domains (e.g. Stape).
Show a read-only preview of exactly what is injected. Changes apply instantly (cache-busted), no deploy needed.
Also provide optional direct fields (used only if GTM is off): GA4 measurement ID, Meta Pixel ID, TikTok Pixel ID, Google Ads conversion ID/label, Microsoft UET tag ID.
Initialise window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [] before the GTM snippet. Support Google Consent Mode v2 defaults from the cookie banner settings.
9.2 dataLayer events (GA4 ecommerce format)
Before every ecommerce event push { ecommerce: null }. Every event includes a unique event_id (UUID or <event>.<timestamp>.<random>) for browser/server deduplication. Currency BDT. Item objects:

{
  "item_id": "HN-500",
  "item_name": "Sundarban Natural Honey",
  "item_brand": "<STORE_NAME>",
  "item_category": "Honey",
  "item_variant": "500 g",
  "price": 850,
  "discount": 140,
  "quantity": 1,
  "index": 0
}
Event	Fires when	Payload
page_view	Every page load and client-side route change	page_type (home, category, product, cart, checkout, thank_you, page, search), page_location, page_title, user_id if logged in, customer_type (new/returning)
view_item	Product page viewed	ecommerce: {currency, value, items:[1]}
add_to_cart	Add to cart, Order now, Buy now, qty increase, bundle add	ecommerce: {currency, value, items} (only the quantity added)
view_cart	Cart page or cart drawer opened	ecommerce: {currency, value, items}
remove_from_cart	Item removed or qty decreased	ecommerce: {currency, value, items} (quantity removed)
begin_checkout	Checkout page opened	ecommerce: {currency, value, coupon, items}
add_shipping_info	Delivery area selected	ecommerce: {currency, value, coupon, shipping_tier, items}
add_payment_info	Payment method selected	ecommerce: {currency, value, coupon, payment_type, items}
purchase	Thank-you page, once per order (guard against reloads)	ecommerce: {transaction_id, value, tax, shipping, discount, currency, coupon, items} + user_data
Also push (recommended extras): view_item_list, select_item, search, add_to_wishlist, sign_up, login, generate_lead (newsletter).

purchase example:

dataLayer.push({ ecommerce: null });
dataLayer.push({
  event: "purchase",
  event_id: "order_10249_purchase",
  ecommerce: {
    transaction_id: "10249",
    value: 1920, tax: 0, shipping: 70, discount: 0,
    currency: "BDT", coupon: "",
    items: [ /* item objects */ ]
  },
  user_data: {
    phone_number: "+8801711482910",
    email: "rahim@gmail.com",
    address: { first_name: "Rahim", last_name: "Uddin", city: "Dhaka", country: "BD" }
  }
});
The browser purchase uses the same event_id pattern as the server Purchase (order_<id>_purchase) so Meta/TikTok can deduplicate. Provide a ready-to-import GTM container JSON (variables, triggers, GA4 event tags) and a TRACKING.md explaining the setup.

9.3 Click ID and attribution capture
On every landing, read URL parameters and cookies, store them in first-party cookies (90 days) and in the session, and attach them to the cart, incomplete order and order:

Field	Platform	Source	Format / rule
fbc	Meta	Built from fbclid URL param, or read _fbc cookie	fb.1.<unix_ms_when_first_seen>.<fbclid>. If a new fbclid arrives, rebuild it; if the same fbclid, keep the original timestamp. Never modify the fbclid value. (It is fbc, not "abc".)
fbp	Meta	_fbp cookie; if missing, create fb.1.<unix_ms>.<random 10-digit>	
fbclid	Meta	URL param	raw, for reference
ttclid	TikTok	URL param / ttclid cookie	raw
ttp	TikTok	_ttp cookie	raw
gclid	Google Ads	URL param / _gcl_aw cookie	raw
gbraid	Google Ads (iOS app→web)	URL param / _gcl_gb	raw
wbraid	Google Ads (iOS web→web)	URL param	raw
msclkid	Microsoft Ads	URL param / _uetmsclkid	raw
twclid	X (Twitter) Ads	URL param	raw
li_fat_id	LinkedIn Ads	URL param	raw
ScCid	Snapchat Ads	URL param / _scid	raw
epik	Pinterest Ads	URL param / _epik	raw
Also store: utm_source, utm_medium, utm_campaign, utm_content, utm_term, utm_id, first-touch and last-touch landing page and timestamp, referrer, client IP (respect proxies/Cloudflare CF-Connecting-IP), user agent, and device type. Show all of it on the order screen.

9.4 Conversion webhook, sent on order CONFIRMATION (not at checkout)
Admin → Settings → Conversion webhook:

Enable toggle; Endpoint URL (HTTPS only; you may add several endpoints, each with its own events and on/off); signing secret (auto-generated, regenerate button).
Events: Confirmed → Purchase (default on), Delivered → OrderDelivered, Cancelled/Returned after confirmation → OrderCancelled, optional Placed → OrderPlaced (off by default).
Option: include SHA-256 hashed user data (normalised per Meta/Google rules: lowercase, trimmed, phone in E.164 without + for hashing).
Send test event button; delivery log (time, order, event, endpoint, HTTP status, duration, attempts, request/response body viewer, retry button).
Delivery via the job queue with retries: 1 min, 5 min, 30 min, 2 h, 12 h (then marked failed and shown on the dashboard). Idempotent: the same event_id on every retry and resend.
Headers: Content-Type: application/json, X-Store-Event: Purchase, X-Store-Signature: sha256=<HMAC_SHA256(raw_body, secret)>, X-Store-Timestamp, Idempotency-Key: <event_id>.
